{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "_comment": "AGENT-11 default Claude Code settings. Hooks below are advisory by default — they run linters/typecheckers and output results, but do not block edits. To promote a hook to blocking, change `|| true` at the end of its command to `|| exit 2`. To disable a hook entirely, remove its entry from the array.",
  "_comment_permissions": "Read-only gates (Sprint 6a): an agent must not edit the criteria that judge its own work. SCOPE, stated exactly: the four deny rules below cover .quality-gates.json anywhere in the tree, plus a gates/ or .gates/ directory AT THE REPO ROOT (Edit(gates/**) is root-anchored, so a nested packages/api/gates/ is NOT covered — add a rule for it if you have one). A test elsewhere that serves as acceptance criteria is covered by NO rule; agents are instructed not to edit it, and nothing refuses them. To intentionally change a gate, edit the file as a deliberate human action with these rules temporarily removed; never let an agent do it mid-mission. A11-ISS-7: Claude Code matches ONLY Edit(path) permission rules for file tools — an Edit rule covers every file-editing tool (Edit, Write, MultiEdit, NotebookEdit), while Write(path)/MultiEdit(path) rule forms are ignored with a session-start warning. The deny list therefore uses Edit() forms only; this is empirically verified to block Write-tool file creation on gate paths. Sprint 6c note: the Edit deny rules do NOT cover Bash, so a PreToolUse 'read-only gate guard' hook blocks the common Bash write forms (redirection, tee, sed -i, cp, mv, rm, truncate, shred, unlink, dd of=, ln -s, perl/ruby -i) to gate paths. It does NOT close the Bash route and must not be described as doing so (A11-ISS-16): a write through an interpreter (python3 -c \"open(path,'w')\") or via variable indirection passes straight through, and no shell guard can catch those. Treat the hook as a speed bump against the accidental; the enforceable guarantee is the Edit() deny rules above. A11-ISS-4: the guard decision lives in .claude/hooks/gate-guard.sh (deployed by install.sh), which inspects the actual Bash command from stdin — the previous hook 'if' glob filter fails open on complex commands (multi-line loops, redirections) and blocked unrelated Bash. If the script is absent the hook allows everything (fail-open by design; the Edit deny rules above still hold).",
  "env": {
    "ENABLE_TOOL_SEARCH": "auto"
  },
  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Edit(.quality-gates.json)",
      "Edit(**/*.quality-gates.json)",
      "Edit(gates/**)",
      "Edit(.gates/**)"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|MultiEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Edit(*.ts|*.tsx)|Write(*.ts|*.tsx)|MultiEdit(*.ts|*.tsx)",
            "command": "command -v npx >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -f package.json ] && [ -f tsconfig.json ] && npx --no-install tsc --noEmit 2>&1 || true",
            "statusMessage": "tsc --noEmit",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Edit(*.py)|Write(*.py)|MultiEdit(*.py)",
            "command": "command -v ruff >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -f pyproject.toml ] && ruff check 2>&1 || true",
            "statusMessage": "ruff check",
            "timeout": 30
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Edit(*.rb)|Write(*.rb)|MultiEdit(*.rb)",
            "command": "command -v rubocop >/dev/null 2>&1 && [ -f Gemfile ] && rubocop --force-exclusion 2>&1 || true",
            "statusMessage": "rubocop",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "prompt",
            "if": "Bash(rm -rf *)|Bash(git push --force*)|Bash(git push -f *)|Bash(git reset --hard*)|Bash(git clean -f*)|Bash(git branch -D*)",
            "prompt": "This command is destructive and hard to reverse. Confirm to proceed: $ARGUMENTS",
            "timeout": 60
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "if [ -f .claude/hooks/gate-guard.sh ]; then sh .claude/hooks/gate-guard.sh; fi",
            "statusMessage": "read-only gate guard",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
